  <bioghist id="b7c57c2ba89bca5971ef278cdafcfdf3">
    <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
<p>Mora McLean joined the Ford Foundation in 1986 as a program officer for the Minority Rights and Opportunities office within the Human Rights and Social Justice program. The Minority Rights and Opportunities program aimed to improve minority access to employment, education, housing, and the political process, by supporting civil rights organizations engaged in litigation, education, and advocacy. In 1990, she became a representative to the West Africa/Nigeria office in Lagos, and in 1995, she became Deputy Director of Africa and Middle East Programs. She left the Foundation in 1996 to become President/CEO for the Africa-America Institute (AAI).</p>  </bioghist>
  <scopecontent id="e397333364f34bd9cd14cdd42a7595e7">
    <head>Scope and Contents</head>
<p>The collection contains correspondence, trip itineraries, inter-office memos, files related to trustee meetings, reports, and grant-related materials.</p>  </scopecontent>
